title: binary ninja plugins and extensions
url:   https://docs.binary.ninja/dev/plugins.html
tags:  binaryninja binja bn python api plugin extension command menu background-task binaryview-type loader render-layer flowgraph transform

; UPPERCASE words are placeholders. Plugins live in user_plugin_path(); restart to load new ones.

## plugin layout
MYPLUGIN/__init__.py                # entry file run when Binary Ninja loads the plugin folder  @layout  <https://docs.binary.ninja/dev/plugins.html#creating-the-plugin>
MYPLUGIN/plugin.json                # metadata for the extension manager (name, version, minimumbinaryninjaversion...)  @manifest  <https://docs.binary.ninja/dev/plugins.html#plugin-description-display>
MYPLUGIN/requirements.txt           # Python packages the extension manager installs for the plugin  @pip @dependencies  <https://docs.binary.ninja/dev/plugins.html#creating-the-plugin>
user_plugin_path()                  # get the folder for your own plugins  @install  <https://api.binary.ninja/index.html#binaryninja.user_plugin_path>
importlib.reload(MOD); MOD.run(bv)  # reload plugin code in the console while you work on it  @iterate @test  <https://docs.binary.ninja/dev/plugins.html#testing>
https://github.com/Vector35/sample_plugin  # template plugin to start from  @example  <https://github.com/Vector35/sample_plugin>
https://github.com/Vector35/binaryninja-api/tree/dev/python/examples  # official Python plugin examples  <https://github.com/Vector35/binaryninja-api/tree/dev/python/examples>

## plugin commands (menu entries)
PluginCommand.register("Menu\\Name", "DESC", FN)  # add a menu command; FN(bv)  @action  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.PluginCommand.register>
PluginCommand.register_for_address("NAME", "DESC", FN)  # add a command run on the cursor address; FN(bv, addr)  @menu  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.PluginCommand.register_for_address>
PluginCommand.register_for_range("NAME", "DESC", FN)  # add a command run on the selection; FN(bv, addr, length)  @menu  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.PluginCommand.register_for_range>
PluginCommand.register_for_function("NAME", "DESC", FN)  # add a command run on the current function; FN(bv, func)  @menu  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.PluginCommand.register_for_function>
PluginCommand.register_for_high_level_il_instruction(N, D, FN)  # add a command on an HLIL instruction; FN(bv, instr)  @menu  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.PluginCommand.register_for_high_level_il_instruction>
PluginCommand.register_for_medium_level_il_function(N, D, FN)  # add a command on an MLIL function; FN(bv, mlil)  @menu  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.PluginCommand.register_for_medium_level_il_function>
PluginCommand.register_global("NAME", "DESC", FN)  # add a command that needs no open file; FN() takes no args  @menu  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.PluginCommand.register_global>
PluginCommand.register_for_project("NAME", "DESC", FN)  # add a command run on a project; FN(project)  @menu  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.PluginCommand.register_for_project>
PluginCommand.register("NAME", "DESC", FN, is_valid=CHECK)  # show a command only when CHECK(bv) is True  @enable  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.PluginCommand.register>
"Group\\Sub\\Name"  # put a command in a sub menu by using backslashes in its name  @submenu @folder  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.PluginCommand.register>
PluginCommand.get_valid_list(PluginCommandContext(bv))  # list commands valid in a context, by name  @invoke @call  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.PluginCommand.get_valid_list>
    ctx = PluginCommandContext(bv); ctx.address = here
    PluginCommand.get_valid_list(ctx)["My Plugin"].execute(ctx)
UIAction.registerAction("NAME", QKeySequence("F3"))  # make a UI action with a hotkey (binaryninjaui, UI only)  @shortcut  <https://docs.binary.ninja/dev/cookbook.html#apply-a-hotkey-to-a-register_-plugin>
UIActionHandler.globalActions().bindAction("NAME", UIAction(FN))  # bind code to a UI action; FN(ctx) gets ctx.binaryView  @hotkey  <https://docs.binary.ninja/dev/cookbook.html#apply-a-hotkey-to-a-register_-plugin>
Menu.mainMenu("Plugins").addAction("NAME", "GROUP")  # put a UI action into a menu  <https://docs.binary.ninja/dev/cookbook.html#apply-a-hotkey-to-a-register_-plugin>

## background work
class Task(BackgroundTaskThread):    # run long work off the UI thread with a status bar entry  @async @progress  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.BackgroundTaskThread>
    class Task(BackgroundTaskThread):
        def __init__(self, bv):
            super().__init__("Working...", can_cancel=True); self.bv = bv
        def run(self):
            for i, f in enumerate(self.bv.functions):
                if self.cancelled: break
                self.progress = f"Working... {i}"
            self.finish()
    Task(bv).start()
task.progress = "TEXT"               # update the text shown in the status bar  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.BackgroundTask.progress>
task.cancelled                       # check whether the user pressed cancel  @stop  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.BackgroundTask.cancelled>
task.finish()                        # mark the task as done and remove it from the status bar  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.BackgroundTask.finish>
task.join()                          # wait for a BackgroundTaskThread to finish  @headless  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.BackgroundTaskThread.join>
BackgroundTask("TEXT", can_cancel=True)  # make a status bar task you update yourself (no thread)  @progress  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.plugin-module.html#binaryninja.plugin.BackgroundTask>
execute_on_main_thread_and_wait(FN)  # run UI code safely from a worker thread  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.mainthread-module.html#binaryninja.mainthread.execute_on_main_thread_and_wait>
with bv.undoable_transaction():      # group a plugin's changes into one undo step  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.undoable_transaction>

## custom file format (binaryview type)
class MyView(BinaryView):     # start a loader for a new file format; set name and long_name  @parser  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView>
    class MyView(BinaryView):
        name = "MyFmt"; long_name = "My Format"
        def __init__(self, data):
            BinaryView.__init__(self, parent_view=data, file_metadata=data.file)
            self.platform = Architecture["armv7"].standalone_platform
        @classmethod
        def is_valid_for_data(cls, data):
            return data.read(0, 4) == b"MYFT"
        def init(self):
            self.add_auto_segment(0x8000, 0x1000, 0x40, 0x1000,
                SegmentFlag.SegmentReadable | SegmentFlag.SegmentExecutable)
            self.add_auto_section(".text", 0x8000, 0x1000, SectionSemantics.ReadOnlyCodeSectionSemantics)
            self.add_entry_point(0x8000)
            return True
        def perform_get_entry_point(self): return 0x8000
        def perform_is_executable(self): return True
    MyView.register()
is_valid_for_data(cls, data)  # return True if the raw data is your format (check magic bytes)  @detect  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryViewType.is_valid_for_data>
init(self)                    # build segments, sections, symbols and entry points; return True on success  @loader  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.init>
self.add_auto_segment(ADDR, LEN, FILE_OFF, FILE_LEN, FLAGS)  # map file bytes into memory from a loader  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.add_auto_segment>
self.add_auto_section(NAME, ADDR, LEN, SEMANTICS)  # add a section from a loader  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.add_auto_section>
self.define_auto_symbol(Symbol(SymbolType.FunctionSymbol, ADDR, "name"))  # add a symbol from a loader  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.define_auto_symbol>
self.add_entry_point(ADDR)    # add an analysis start point from a loader  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.add_entry_point>
perform_get_entry_point / perform_is_executable / perform_get_address_size  # override basic file facts in a custom view  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.perform_get_entry_point>
MyView.register()             # make the format show up in the open-with list  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.register>
get_load_settings_for_data(cls, data)  # offer load options (image base, arch) for your format  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryViewType.get_load_settings_for_data>
bv.record_imported_object_library(LIB, NAME, ADDR)  # record which type library an import came from (in loaders)  @imports  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.binaryview-module.html#binaryninja.binaryview.BinaryView.record_imported_object_library>

## render layers (change how code looks)
class Layer(RenderLayer):           # change rendered lines of disassembly/IL; set name, override apply_to_*  @render  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.renderlayer-module.html#binaryninja.renderlayer.RenderLayer>
    class HighlightRet(RenderLayer):
        name = "Highlight Returns"
        def apply_to_high_level_il_body(self, function, lines):
            for line in lines:
                if any(t.text == "return" for t in line.contents.tokens):
                    line.contents.highlight = HighlightColor(red=0, green=80, blue=0)
            return lines
    HighlightRet.register()
apply_to_block(self, block, lines)  # change lines of any basic block (asm, LLIL, MLIL)  @render  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.renderlayer-module.html#binaryninja.renderlayer.RenderLayer.apply_to_block>
apply_to_high_level_il_body(self, function, lines)  # change lines of a whole HLIL function  @render  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.renderlayer-module.html#binaryninja.renderlayer.RenderLayer.apply_to_high_level_il_body>
apply_to_flow_graph(self, graph)    # change nodes and edges of a graph view  @render  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.renderlayer-module.html#binaryninja.renderlayer.RenderLayer.apply_to_flow_graph>
Layer.register()                    # make a render layer available (users enable it per view)  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.renderlayer-module.html#binaryninja.renderlayer.RenderLayer.register>

## data renderers (custom data display)
class R(DataRenderer):        # render data of a type your own way in linear view  @struct @display  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.datarender-module.html#binaryninja.datarender.DataRenderer>
    class BarRenderer(DataRenderer):
        def perform_is_valid_for_data(self, ctxt, view, addr, type, context):
            return DataRenderer.is_type_of_struct_name(type, "BAR", context)
        def perform_get_lines_for_data(self, ctxt, view, addr, type, prefix, width, context):
            prefix.append(InstructionTextToken(InstructionTextTokenType.TextToken, "BAR!"))
            return [DisassemblyTextLine(prefix, addr)]
    BarRenderer().register_type_specific()
R().register_type_specific()  # use the renderer before the generic ones  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.datarender-module.html#binaryninja.datarender.DataRenderer.register_type_specific>
R().register_generic()        # use the renderer as a fallback for any type  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.datarender-module.html#binaryninja.datarender.DataRenderer.register_generic>

## flow graphs
g = FlowGraph()                # make an empty custom graph  @diagram  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.flowgraph-module.html#binaryninja.flowgraph.FlowGraph>
n = FlowGraphNode(g); n.lines = ["TEXT"]; g.append(n)  # add a node with text lines  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.flowgraph-module.html#binaryninja.flowgraph.FlowGraphNode>
a.add_outgoing_edge(BranchType.UnconditionalBranch, b)  # connect two nodes (TrueBranch, FalseBranch... set the color)  @arrow  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.flowgraph-module.html#binaryninja.flowgraph.FlowGraphNode.add_outgoing_edge>
a.add_outgoing_edge(TYPE, b, EdgeStyle(EdgePenStyle.DashLine, 2, COLOR))  # connect nodes with a custom line style  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.flowgraph-module.html#binaryninja.flowgraph.EdgeStyle>
n.highlight = HighlightStandardColor.BlueHighlightColor  # color a graph node  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.flowgraph-module.html#binaryninja.flowgraph.FlowGraphNode.highlight>
show_graph_report("TITLE", g)  # show a graph in a new tab  @ui  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.interaction-module.html#binaryninja.interaction.show_graph_report>
g.layout_and_wait()            # compute node positions without the UI (e.g. to export)  @headless  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.flowgraph-module.html#binaryninja.flowgraph.FlowGraph.layout_and_wait>
f.create_graph()               # get the built-in graph of a function to inspect or show  @cfg  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.function-module.html#binaryninja.function.Function.create_graph>

## transforms (encode, decode, hash, unpack)
list(Transform)                      # list transforms (Base64, Zlib, XOR, AES, SHA256, RawHex...)  @encode @decode  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.transform-module.html#binaryninja.transform.Transform>
Transform["Base64"].decode(DATA)     # decode bytes with a transform  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.transform-module.html#binaryninja.transform.Transform.decode>
Transform["Zlib"].decode(DATA)       # decompress zlib data  @inflate  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.transform-module.html#binaryninja.transform.Transform.decode>
Transform["XOR"].decode(DATA, {"key": b"KEY"})  # xor-decode bytes with a key  @decrypt  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.transform-module.html#binaryninja.transform.Transform.decode>
Transform["SHA256"].encode(DATA)     # hash bytes (MD5, SHA1, SHA256...)  @digest  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.transform-module.html#binaryninja.transform.Transform.encode>
Transform["AES-128 CBC"].parameters  # list the parameter names a transform needs (key, iv...)  @decrypt @options  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.transform-module.html#binaryninja.transform.Transform>
class MyT(Transform):                # add your own transform; override perform_decode / perform_encode  @custom  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.transform-module.html#binaryninja.transform.Transform>
TransformSession(PATH)               # open a container (zip, tar.gz, base64...) and extract down to a loadable file  @archive  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.transform-module.html#binaryninja.transform.TransformSession>
    s = TransformSession("archive.tar.gz")
    if s.process():
        s.set_selected_contexts(s.current_context)
        with load(s.current_view) as bv:
            print(bv.file.virtual_path)   # Gzip(...)::Tar()::file
ctx.set_transform_name("Base64"); s.process_from(ctx)  # force a transform when auto-detect fails  @container @manual  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.transform-module.html#binaryninja.transform.TransformContext.set_transform_name>
ctx.available_files / ctx.set_requested_files([NAMES])  # list and pick files inside an archive context  @container  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.transform-module.html#binaryninja.transform.TransformContext.set_requested_files>
DataBuffer(DATA).base64_decode()     # decode base64 with a DataBuffer  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.databuffer-module.html#binaryninja.databuffer.DataBuffer.base64_decode>
DataBuffer(DATA).zlib_decompress()   # inflate zlib data with a DataBuffer  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.databuffer-module.html#binaryninja.databuffer.DataBuffer.zlib_decompress>

## extension manager
RepositoryManager()  # get the plugin repositories manager  @extensions @install  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.extensionmanager-module.html#binaryninja.extensionmanager.RepositoryManager>
RepositoryManager().default_repository.plugins  # list plugins in the official repository  @extensions  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.extensionmanager-module.html#binaryninja.extensionmanager.Repository.plugins>
RepositoryManager().default_repository["PLUGIN_PATH"].install()  # install a plugin from a repository  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.extensionmanager-module.html#binaryninja.extensionmanager.Extension.install>
plugin.enabled = False / plugin.enable()  # turn an installed plugin off or on  @toggle  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.extensionmanager-module.html#binaryninja.extensionmanager.Extension.enabled>
RepositoryManager().check_for_updates()  # check repositories for plugin updates  @update  <https://api.binary.ninja/binaryninja.extensionmanager-module.html#binaryninja.extensionmanager.RepositoryManager.check_for_updates>
